---
import Nav from "@/components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Shellular"
  description="Terms of Service for Shellular — the remote development tool by Shellular."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-container">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <p class="section-label">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="meta">Effective date: April 19, 2026 · Shellular</p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-body">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
          <p>
            By downloading, installing, or using the Shellular mobile app, the Shellular CLI (<code>shellular</code>),
            or any related services (collectively, the "Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service
            ("Terms"). If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
          </p>
          <p>The Service is provided by Shellular ("Company", "we", "us", "our").</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Description of the Service</h2>
          <p>
            Shellular is a developer tool that allows you to connect a mobile device to a development machine you own or
            are authorised to access. The Service comprises:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Shellular CLI</strong> — a host agent you run on your machine that exposes terminal, filesystem, port
              management, and system-monitoring capabilities over an encrypted relay.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Shellular App</strong> — the mobile application you use to connect to a running CLI instance.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Relay Infrastructure</strong> — servers that facilitate encrypted pass-through communication between
              the app and the CLI.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
          <p>
            You must be at least 13 years old (or the minimum age required by your country's laws) to use the Service.
            By using the Service you represent that you meet this requirement.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Permitted Use</h2>
          <p>
            You may use the Service only to access machines that you own or have explicit, authorised permission to
            access. You agree to use the Service in compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
          <p>You agree not to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Use the Service to access any machine without authorisation.</li>
            <li>Use the Service to transmit malware, ransomware, or any other malicious code.</li>
            <li>
              Attempt to reverse-engineer, decompile, or tamper with the relay infrastructure or the encryption layer.
            </li>
            <li>
              Use the Service in any way that could damage, overload, or impair the relay servers or interfere with
              other users' access.
            </li>
            <li>
              Resell, sublicense, or provide access to the relay infrastructure to third parties without our written
              consent.
            </li>
            <li>
              Use the Service for any unlawful purpose, including but not limited to exfiltrating data, conducting
              cyberattacks, or facilitating unauthorized surveillance.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p>
            The Shellular name, logo, and app interface are owned by Shellular. The CLI source code is released under its
            open-source licence (see the repository for details). Nothing in these Terms grants you rights in our
            trademarks or branding.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Your use of the Service is also governed by our
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference. As described
            there, we collect no personal data and all relay traffic is end-to-end encrypted.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>
            Shellular may integrate with third-party AI providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, GitHub, etc.) and your use of
            those integrations is subject to the respective provider's terms and privacy policies. We have no control
            over and assume no responsibility for third-party services.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
          <p>
            THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
            INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND
            NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SERVICE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, ERROR-FREE, OR SECURE.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are solely responsible for the security of the machine(s) you connect via Shellular, including keeping
            the CLI updated, controlling who has physical access to your QR code, and managing the <code>--dir</code> root
            appropriately.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, Shellular AND ITS OFFICERS, EMPLOYEES, AND AFFILIATES WILL
            NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING BUT NOT
            LIMITED TO LOSS OF DATA, LOSS OF PROFITS, OR UNAUTHORISED ACCESS TO YOUR MACHINE, ARISING OUT OF OR IN
            CONNECTION WITH YOUR USE OF THE SERVICE, EVEN IF WE HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
          </p>
          <p>
            OUR TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ANY CLAIMS ARISING UNDER THESE TERMS WILL NOT EXCEED THE AMOUNT YOU
            PAID US IN THE 12 MONTHS PRECEDING THE CLAIM (OR USD 10 IF YOU HAVE NOT MADE ANY PAYMENTS).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Indemnification</h2>
          <p>
            You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Shellular and its officers, directors, employees, and agents from
            any claims, damages, or expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from: (a) your use of the
            Service; (b) your violation of these Terms; or (c) your violation of any third-party rights.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Modifications to the Service and Terms</h2>
          <p>
            We reserve the right to modify or discontinue the Service (or any part of it) at any time with or without
            notice. We may also update these Terms. The effective date at the top of this page will reflect the latest
            revision. Continued use after a revision constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>13. Governing Law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of India, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Any disputes
            arising under these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts located in India.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>14. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about these Terms, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:team@shellular.dev">team@shellular.dev</a>.
          </p>
          <address>
            Shellular<br />
          </address>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    min-height: 80vh;
    padding: 80px clamp(16px, 8vw, 80px) 64px;
  }

  .legal-container {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 56px;
  }

  .legal-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    background: var(--grad-text);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    padding-top: 32px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  ul li {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    padding-left: 18px;
    position: relative;
  }

  ul li::before {
    content: "–";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent2);
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  code {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    background: rgba(var(--brand-gold-rgb), 0.08);
    border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  address {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
